Please open the file readings.csv. It has the columns group, minute and temperature, and the temperatures are in degrees Celsius.

For each group, please show me the average temperature, and also the biggest drop in temperature between two readings that come one after the other.

Then please show me every reading converted to Fahrenheit. To convert, multiply the Celsius temperature by 9, divide by 5, and then add 32.

Finally, please make a line chart of the temperatures for group A over time (minute along the bottom, temperature going up the side) and save it as cooling.svg.

Thank you!
